\"} ! Stargardt disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/14423 {source=\"OMIM:621259\"} ! RDH8\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0980723\nname: fetomaternal alloimmune thrombocytopenia 1\nsubset: inferred_rare\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621264\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: MEDGEN:356917 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:621264 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C1868202 {source=\"MEDGEN:356917\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0019415 {source=\"OMIM:621264\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! fetal and neonatal alloimmune thrombocytopenia\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/6156 {source=\"OMIM:621264\"} ! ITGB3\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0980749\nname: apolipoprotein A-II deficiency\nsubset: inferred_rare\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621417\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: MEDGEN:854810 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: OMIM:621417 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C3888202 {source=\"MEDGEN:854810\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0017773 {source=\"OMIM:621417\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! hypoalphalipoproteinemia\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010000\nname: pythiosis\ndef: \"A granulomatous disease caused by the aquatic organism pythium insidiosum occurring rarely in humans. It is classified into three forms: ocular, cutaneous, and arterial.\" [MESH:D058968] {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\", source=\"PMID:31845178\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0011989\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: mondo_curated_rare {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7697-3026\", source=\"PMID:35205934\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"human pythiosis\" EXACT [GARD:0011989]\nsynonym: \"pythium insidiosum infection\" EXACT [GARD:0011989]\nxref: GARD:0011989 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: icd11.foundation:1571230529 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:124447 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: MESH:D058968 {source=\"MONDO:mondoIsNarrowerThanSource\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0276912 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:124447\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005550 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! infectious disease\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010030\nname: pediatric high-grade glioma\ndef: \"A malignant high-grade glioma that occurs during childhood in the central nervous system.\" [PMID:35456430, PMID:38496580]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027222\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C202298\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"childhood malignant glioma\" EXACT [NCIT:C202298]\nsynonym: \"pHGG\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:35456430, PMID:38496580]\nxref: GARD:0027222 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1861427 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C202298 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5908419 {source=\"MEDGEN:1861427\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0006517 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! childhood malignant neoplasm\nis_a: MONDO:0100342 {source=\"NCIT:C202298\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! malignant glioma\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8126\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010100\nname: myxedema coma\ndef: \"A rare complication of hypothyroidism characterized by altered mental status, hypothermia, and symptoms related to the slowing of other organ systems.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK545193/, PMID:33083180, PMID:34194879, PMID:38279788]\ncomment: Hypothyroid patients exhibit multiple physiologic alterations to compensate for the deficiency of thyroid hormone. Acute stressors like infection, myocardial infarction, cold exposure, and surgery in patients with poorly controlled hypothyroidism can overwhelm these homeostatic mechanisms and can lead to myxedema coma. It can also occur as a culmination of severe, longstanding hypothyroidism. PMID:34194879, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK545193/\nxref: MEDGEN:536791 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0238298 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:536791\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005420 {source=\"PMID:33083180\", source=\"PMID:34194879\", source=\"PMID:38279788\"} ! hypothyroidism\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8513\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010108\nname: myxedema heart disease\ndef: \"A rare complication of hypothyroidism characterized by unexplained heart failure refractory to conventional treatment.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:30277162, PMID:36225224]\ncomment: Myxedema heart disease is a potentially fatal syndrome that encompasses an enlarged cardiac silhouette, pericardial effusions, and electrocardiographic change: bradycardia, low-voltage, conduction blocks, ST changes, T-wave inversions, and arrhythmias. It is is potentially reversible with thyroid hormone (TH) administration. PMID:36225224\nxref: MEDGEN:526137 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0221048 {source=\"MEDGEN:526137\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005420 {source=\"PMID:30277162\", source=\"PMID:36225224\"} ! hypothyroidism\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8513\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010111\nname: loin pain hematuria syndrome\ndef: \"A rare and debilitating renal pain disorder characterized by chronic, severe loin pain with or without micro- or macroscopic hematuria.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:30984919, PMID:33532147, PMID:38106595]\ncomment: The condition may be classified into type 1 LPHS, which has identifiable causes and type 2 LPHS, in which no clear underlying etiology is found. PMID:30984919, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\nsynonym: \"LPHS\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:30984919]\nxref: MEDGEN:78696 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0268712 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:78696\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0024317 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! chronic pain syndrome\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8410\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010117\nname: sudden unexplained death in childhood\ndef: \"The sudden unexpected death of a person age 1 to 18 years that remains unexplained after a thorough case investigation, including performance of a complete autopsy with ancillary testing, and review of the clinical history and circumstances of death.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6694-3699, PMID:31502215]\nxref: MEDGEN:820021 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C3827273 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:820021\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1010120 {source=\"PMID:28679642\"} ! sudden unexpected death in pediatrics\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8635\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010122\nname: trichrome vitiligo\ndef: \"Any form of vitiligo characterized by a tan zone of varying width between normal and depigmented skin. This intermediate tan zone has more inflammatory cells, Langerhans cells, and melanophages than vitiliginous or normal skin. The number of melanocytes is greater than in vitiliginous skin but fewer than in normal skin.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473, PMID:21839315]\nxref: MEDGEN:697977 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: SCTID:403270009 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C1274649 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:697977\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0008661 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\"} ! vitiligo\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8542\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010125\nname: generalized vitiligo\ndef: \"Any form of vitiligo characterized by loss of pigment (depigmentation) in patches of skin all over the body.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473, PMID:28317523, PMID:32644575]\nsynonym: \"generalised vitiligo\" EXACT OMO:0003005 [PMID:16015369]\nsynonym: \"mixed vitiligo\" EXACT [PMID:28317523]\nxref: MEDGEN:725821 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C1304470 {source=\"MEDGEN:725821\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0008661 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\"} ! vitiligo\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8541\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010128\nname: peritonitis\ndef: \"Inflammation of the peritoneum (tissue that lines the abdominal wall and covers most of the organs in the abdomen).\" [https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmedhealth/PMHT0022963/]\ncomment: Peritonitis can result from infection, injury, or certain diseases. Symptoms may include swelling of the abdomen, severe pain, and weight loss. https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmedhealth/PMHT0022963/\nsynonym: \"peritoneum inflammation\" EXACT [icd11.foundation:775356003, MONDO:patterns/inflammatory_disease_by_site]\nxref: ICD10WHO:K65 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7941-5545\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9439-5346\"}\nxref: icd11.foundation:775356003 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:14697 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: MESH:D010538 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1967-3726\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0031154 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:14697\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0021166 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! inflammatory disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700096 ! human disease\nintersection_of: disease_has_inflammation_site UBERON:0002358 ! peritoneum\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8539\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010131\nname: encapsulating peritoneal sclerosis\ndef: \"A debilitating condition characterized by a fibrocollagenous membrane encasing the small intestine, resulting in recurrent small bowel obstructions.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK574525/, PMID:24133081, PMID:30065556, PMID:39631118]\ncomment: EPS is most commonly associated with long-term peritoneal dialysis, though medications, peritoneal infection, and systemic inflammatory disorders have been implicated. Many cases remain idiopathic. PMID:30065556\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:696175\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:696175\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:696175\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"abdominal cocoon syndrome\" EXACT [Orphanet:696175, PMID:30065556]\nsynonym: \"EPS\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [Orphanet:696175, PMID:30065556]\nsynonym: \"peritonitis chronica fibrosa incapsulata\" EXACT [PMID:30065556]\nsynonym: \"sclerosing encapsulating peritonitis\" EXACT [icd11.foundation:1269928839, Orphanet:696175, PMID:3006555