ision, typically appearing in people between the ages of 50 and 60. It is characterized by the dilation and leakage of blood vessels in the macula, the part of the retina responsible for sharp, detailed vision, and is also linked to neurodegeneration in retinal cells.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, https://www.aao.org/eye-health/diseases/macular-telangiectasia, PMID:36237488]\nsynonym: \"MacTel type 2\" EXACT [PMID:23510315]\nsynonym: \"MacTel2\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767]\nxref: MEDGEN:1690677 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5232269 {source=\"MEDGEN:1690677\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1010184 {source=\"PMID:38059108\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! macular telangiectasia\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9755\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010184\nname: macular telangiectasia\ndef: \"An eye disorder characterized by retinal capillary network incompetence, dilatations, and thinning which can be uniocular or binocular and causes gradual deterioration of central vision.\" [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macular_telangiectasia, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, PMID:38059108]\nxref: MEDGEN:573180 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0339480 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:573180\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005328 {source=\"PMID:38059108\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! eye disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9755\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1010185\nname: transplant rejection\ndef: \"A disease related to transplantation that occurs when transplant tissue is rejected 